# Bilingual parity policy

Arabic and English guides ship together.

- Every `README_AR.md` (or `*_AR.md`) must have a sibling English file with the same base name: `README_AR.md` → `README.md` in the same directory.
- Both files must cover the same sections in the same order. Headings, tables, and citation numbers must match one-to-one.
- Do not machine-translate a regulatory claim. Translate the explanation, keep the GACAR citation exactly as in the English source, and verify the Arabic wording against the official Arabic publication where one exists.
- When you add a section to the English file, add it to the Arabic file in the same change; never leave the pair out of step.
- `node scripts/gate.mjs` must report zero `bilingual` findings before a content PR is ready.
